{
  "doc": "What happens to an arrow once a person has dragged it. originAtFirstPoint's first two cases are real: the arrow the-bastion's Workshop page painted for the Kubernetes engagement's DF32 (ci_fetch_jobs), read off the canvas after convertToExcalidrawElements, and DF31 (ci_clone) as Excalidraw 0.18.1 left it after one drag of its end point (2026-09-28) — the stray [0.5,-0.5] grown to [2048,-2048]. releaseEnds and reboundEnds cases mirror the rules the-bastion's backend applies on Save (an end more than 40px off its box put back to the router's anchor; an end bound to another component, any part of a multi-element symbol, proposed as a re-pointing). reboundEnds is compared EXACTLY (an absent key is the answer), not tolerantly.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "fn": "originAtFirstPoint",
      "name": "a doubly bound arrow as the converter hands it back is moved onto its first point",
      "element": {
        "type": "arrow",
        "x": 1814.104989685931,
        "y": 761.0463332082364,
        "points": [
          [
            0.5,
            -0.5
          ],
          [
            106.25692890573373,
            -204.7757031565128
          ]
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "type": "arrow",
        "x": 1814.60499,
        "y": 760.546333,
        "points": [
          [
            0,
            0
          ],
          [
            105.756929,
            -204.275703
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "fn": "originAtFirstPoint",
